Hi there, everybody!
Here's the latest update to Anthropomachy.
In version 1.20 we are introducing several new events as well as some minor bug fixes.

We want to thank you all from the huge amounts of feedback we have received. We hope with this update we are making the game even more enjoyable for you.

Here's what we've updated in this version:

 - New god-specific events;
 - Fixed bug when unlocking certain achievements;
 - Fixed bug when displaying the End Game screen;
 - Fixed several minor bugs and typing errors;

Other than bug fixes, this will be the [url=http://toyboxlab.com/closing-points-of-2019/]last planned update[/url] we will release for Anthropomachy. 
Once again, thank you all for your love and help. There's plenty more to come from us as we'll begin working on our next project right away, so keep an eye out on social media ([url=https://www.facebook.com/toyboxlab]Facebook[/url] - [url=https://twitter.com/TheToyBoxLab]Twitter[/url] - [url=https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCHMqVy-_n_PpTMW4Rs2bZ6A]YouTube[/url] - [url=https://www.instagram.com/toyboxlab/]Instagram[/url] - [url=https://www.reddit.com/r/Anthropomachy/]Reddit[/url]) and [url=http://toyboxlab.com/blog/]our blog[/url] for what's next!

Hi there, everybody!
This is the first update for Anthropomachy since our release last week.
We want to thank you ALL for showing interest in our game, the response has been much bigger that we ever expected!

A special thanks to everybody who took the time to send us their feedbacks on our Steam forum and social media, most of the updates we're bringing here today are based on what you guys are sending us so, keep them coming!

Also, we ask that if you enjoyed the game, please write a positive review!
Since we're a small company (two people) with no marketing budget, we depend solely on our review score to have any visibility on Steam.
On the other hand, if you found a problem with the game we ask you to please give us a chance to fix it before writing a negative review. Send us a message on [url=https://steamcommunity.com/app/1018270/discussions/]our forum [/url]or social media and we will look into it.
Help us make Anthropomachy even better!

Heads up: DO NOT use save files from older versions as these will not work properly with this update.

Here's what we've updated in this version:

 - Reduced every ability cooldown in half;
 - Temples now may allow for an ability accuracy to reach 100%;
 - Changed skepticism impact for most events;
 - Skepticism will now only affect your followers at 40% (previously 25%);
 - Increased the number of errors needed to increase Skepticism (previously skepticism would rise 1% for every 3 errors, now it takes 5);
 - New credits video featuring all gods;

We hope you enjoy what this update brings and if you find any issues, you know [url=https://steamcommunity.com/app/1018270/discussions/]where to find us![/url]

It's here! The official release of Anthropomachy!
8 new mighty gods descend from the Olympus to join the effort to reconquer XXI Century Earth!
But this version also includes some other great changes like a new country receptivity mechanic, keyboard navigation and much more!

Here's the list of everything that has been changed for version 1.0:

 - 8 new Major Gods;

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/34985080/6314c78078b8a8f6085232653a45da5db2c9915c.png[/img]

 - New religious presence and country receptivity mechanic;

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/34985080/2f3351b913cf7c66b2bd62c18243eb6e8b87041c.png[/img]

 - Keyboard (WASD) navigation;
 - Included information of ability traits on the details screen;

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/34985080/9b99beec9d7f0ac6e1ea1400e7b1b091b32539e3.png[/img]

 - Included Loading messages;
 - Increased trait upgrades to 10% (was 5%);
 - Decreased preacher cost to 200 faith (was 250);
 - Added many new events related to the 8 new Major Gods;
 - Fixed UI placement in smaller resolutions;
 - Fixed bug that allowed the purchase of powers from more than one secondary god;
 - Fixed bug that froze gameplay if multiple UI windows appeared during the same frame;
 - Fixed bug that reduced the number of available preachers if loading the skill tree with a temple selected;
 - Fixed typos in certain events and news (let us know if you found any errors!)
 - Fixed news bug that didn't allow the camera travel to Libya on click;
 - Fixed value on certain event special options;
 - Fixed bug that froze the game when calling end game from an event error;
 - General balancing improvements;

We want to thank every one that supported and sent us their feedback during our Early Access. 
If you were one of the early adopters you know how much Anthropomachy has evolved during these 5 months and it was all due to your help.
But know that the work isn't done. We still plan to add more content to the game and will, obviously, still fix any remaining bug ou guys might find.

Thanks once again for all the love we've gotten during these past months and a special thanks to everyone that visited our booth during BGS 2019! It was a blast to talk to each and every one of you and know what you guys think about Anthropomachy!

On our blog post about this update we also did some reminiscing about the development process, so please [url=http://toyboxlab.com/anthropomachys-official-release/]check it out[/url]!
Also, please follow us on social media, Anthropomachy is just the first step in this journey and many more awesome games still lie in the future.

How are you doing, guys and girls? Today we introduce to you the all-new all-improved Anthopomachy v0.40!
I know we said this a couple of times but once again, this is the biggest update to Anthropomachy ever! And, as with every major update: Old save files won't work!

We talked a bit about it in a [url=http://toyboxlab.com/10-the-dev-lab-improving-anthropomachy-through-early-access/]blog post[/url] a couple of weeks ago and  now it's finally here!

Now, the very long list of everything that has been changed on this version:

 - New Conversion/Skepticism bar showing the current state of your conquering effort and your goals;
 - Added Temple mechanic where building a temple on a given country will cost you more than one preacher;
 - Country attributes now have 4 different colors depending on their current level;
 - Adopted country's real population numbers as conversion metric;
 - Map and bars now appear in a custom color for each god;
 - Fixed and added new SFX when casting abilities and upgrading traits on the Skill Tree;
 - Added simple VFXs when casting abilities;
 - New Culture icon;
 - Added new Faith and Preacher icons;
 - No longer showing World Conversion on the country bar when no country is selected;
 - Included a border when hovering for countries that already have temples built;
 - Reduced the incidence of error on most abilities;
 - Overhauled the ability cooldown system;
 - New and more detailed ability window;
 - New and more detailed event option window;
 - Added effect of event decision on event result window;
 - Reduced ability accuracy bonus per temple from 10% to 1%;
 - Reduced the skepticism impact of consecutive ability errors from 5% to 1%;
 - Raised the country conversion limit per affected attribute from 10% to 15%;
 - Honor bonus reduced from 1.5x - 4x to 1x - 3x;
 - Honor level and population multiplier are now disconsidered when casting an ability on a country with ineffective attributes;
 - Honor bonus now runs parallel with the ability type. Curses with have bonus with low honor and Blessings with high honor;
 - Added specific error message when casting abilities with opposite effects on the same country;
 - Fixed a bug on the Ability Hit method that allowed for an ability to have a higher accuracy than excepected;
 - Balancing adjustments;
 - General performance improvements;
 - Fixed UI bugs on older monitors;
 - Fixed bug that caused crash when player ran out of events;
 - Updated the tutorial;

Ok, that was a lot. But the big changes are the improved UI and the new Conversion/Skepticism bar. We feel both of those will enhance your experience giving more detailed information and overall helping the flow of the game.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/34985080/0bce89c65444bdb2361f93e360089d35facfde29.png[/img]

The idea for the bar is simple, If the bar reaches [b]75% conversion, you've won![/b] If skepticism gets to [b]50% before that, you've lost[/b].
Also, once you reach 50% conversion you will also start converting some skeptics and, on the other hand, if Skepticism reaches 25%, you'll start losing some previously-converted followers as well.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/34985080/a95346ef468a224cd34670616ace6b43f538c6ae.png[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/34985080/1a67b335d28d9319d8b4eb3be1cbdcad5afa1182.png[/img]
The new Conversion/Skepticism bar showing you the win/loss scenarios

We've also updated the UI for the ability and event details window. Now you should have even more control over how a specific ability will work and better manage your strategy.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/34985080/9be13f80fe629ef3734e3e0f44882c7dcf258211.png[/img]
The new ability details window

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/34985080/c0d6065931cde8319a47e2d6c90afe5d612b1e5b.png[/img]
The new event details window

Notice that abilities now have a cooldown period so plan their usage accordingly.
In this effort to give you more information we've also changed the countries attributes to the following scale:
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/34985080/105c5eabe11d599126f46904fbcf2258ddf81bb0.png[/img]

We hope all these changes will give you a better feeling of control when conquering Earth and allow for better planning your strategy. 

On a side note, as we've mentioned on our [url=http://toyboxlab.com/10-the-dev-lab-improving-anthropomachy-through-early-access/]blog post[/url], we're also very excited to announce that we'll be at Brazil Game Show on Oct 9th - 13th! So if you happen to attend the event, come visit us on our booth!

Soon we'll announce the official release date for the game as well as the remaining main gods. Here's a (heavily edited as to not make it obvious) sneak peek:
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/34985080/7bf907ee8a15b04e73c44023265ada6231e2b752.png[/img]

As always, keep playing Anthropomachy, keep sending us your feedback as they are the only way we can make the game better for you!

First of all, we want to thank everybody who sent us their first impressions of the game. They were incredibly valuable and we look forward to keep improving Anthropomachy until the official launch!

Here's what we are changing with this update:

- We added a tutorial for everyone playing the game for the first time. You can disable it by completing the tutorial or going to Main Menu -> Options -> Hide Tutorial;
- Fixed some news that had special characters;
- Fixed the bug where the game volume was at 100% when the game first booted up;
- Fixed a bug that caused a high frame rate in the Skill Tree

Please, keep playing and reporting your impressions and every bug you find. All suggestions and criticisms are extremely welcome so we can together make Anthropomachy an awesome game!

See you soon!
